    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A sailor from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nice">Nice</a> drawn into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-mazzini">Giuseppe Mazzini</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/young-italy">Young Italy</a>, Garibaldi was sentenced to death after a failed rising in 1834 and spent 14 years in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>, fighting for the Ragamuffins in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> and raising the Redshirts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a>.</li><li>Back in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> he defended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a> in 1849 and then, setting his republicanism aside for the Sardinian monarchy, led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/expedition-of-the-thousand">Expedition of the Thousand</a> in 1860, which won <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> for the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a>.</li><li>His attempts to take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> from the pope failed at Aspromonte in 1862 and Mentana in 1867; anti-papal and later a supporter of the Paris Commune, he became an international symbol of national independence and republican ideals.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>When the Union offered him a major general's commission in 1861, Garibaldi said he would serve only as commander-in-chief, with the power to declare the abolition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>. Lincoln was not yet ready to free the slaves, and Garibaldi did not join the Union army.</p></aside>
    </section>

